ate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "  Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "philately"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the name of the activity of collecting stamps"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Philately is a very popular hobby."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le17ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about stamp collecting."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "philatelist"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who collects stamps"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There is no lack of philatelists who collect and trade every type of stamp."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le17ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "theme"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that different things have in common"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some collectors prefer to collect stamps on a certain theme, such as flowers, maps or birds."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le17ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mail"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "documents delivered to your home"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Philatelists eagerly wait for their mail every day. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le17ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stamp"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small piece of paper placed on items sent in the mail as proof of payment"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have the beginning of a stamp collection!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le17ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect vs. Simple Past Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way. <br><br>You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> necessarily connected to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experience. When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">I have learned English</span>  = I learned English in the past and now I can speak English.</span></li><li><span class=\"italic\">He has bought a painting</span> = He bought the painting in the past and now he has a painting. </li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have/has + the past participle</span> of the verb in Present Perfect sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart about how to form the Present Perfect tense:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Participle \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"arrive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"arrived\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"arrived\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A few letters have arrived...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"grow\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"grew\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"grown\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The range of images has grown...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"begin\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"began\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"begun\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have begun...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "A few letters have arrived in the mail.  You have a stamp collection!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Since the 1800s, the range of stamp images has grown. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Quantifiers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item. Quantifiers do not indicate a specific quantity but rather a general amount."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<br><ul><li>You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns.</li> <li>Quantifiers like <span class=\"italic\"> a few, several, many, dozens, hundreds, thousands, or  <span class=\"italic\">millions, can only be used with count nouns.</li> <li>You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Quantifier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a couple<br> a few<br> no/none<br> any /not any<br> some <br>a lot of / lots of  / tons <br>plenty of <br>lack of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"two<br> around three or more<br> 0, nothing<br> to ask about / say there is not<br> a small, general number or amount<br> a very large number or amount<br> more than you need<br> less than you need<br>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Any time a few letters arrive in the mail, you have the beginning of a stamp collection. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "There is no lack of philatelists who collect and trade every type of stamp."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le17ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a special occasion. It can be something in your personal life or something everyone knows about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a sketch of the event. Make it look like it is on a stamp."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a paragraph explaining why this is an important event for you."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your paragraph to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I choose a special occasion."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I design a stamp."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a paragraph of 60 - 80 words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read the paragraph aloud."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can talk about hobbies."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can discuss experiences I've had or haven't had. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about general and specific quantities."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "  Have you ever collected stamps? Would you like to collect stamps? Why or why not?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Would you like to collect stam